==Dialogue==
When approached, she will provide some random information, saying: 
:''"There's a rift here in Skyrim, and can't neither magic nor the passin' of time make it right."''
:''"Evgir Unslaad has come at last. The 'Season Unending.' War... without end."''
:''"Can you believe those pathetic Gray-Manes still show their face in public?"''
:''"There was love between our families. For generations. Now, there is only enmity."''
:''"Do be careful, child. Skyrim is not as safe as it used to be."''
:''"By the way, you might want to stop in at Warmaiden's. These days, folk need all the protection they can get."''

If Whiterun was conquered by the [[Skyrim:Stormcloaks|Stormcloaks]] during [[Skyrim:Battle for Whiterun (Stormcloaks)|Battle for Whiterun]], she will hatefully add: 
:''"It's a miracle these Stormcloaks haven't robbed us blind yet. I'm sure it's only a matter of time."''

==Conversations==
Bergritte suggests [[Skyrim:Lars Battle-Born|Lars]] go play outside:

'''Bergritte:''' ''Lars, dear, why don't you go outside and play? It's a beautiful day.''<br>
'''Lars:''' ''That's all right, grandmother. I like staying home with you.''<br>
'''Bergritte:''' ''It's that Braith girl again, isn't it? Has she been bothering you again? I've a mind to speak with her mother.''<br>
'''Lars:''' ''No! Please, grandmother, don't do that. I'm fine. Really. Can we just... not talk about this anymore?''<br>
'''Bergritte:''' ''All right, dear.''<br>

Bergritte and her daughter, [[Skyrim:Alfhild Battle-Born|Alfhild]], discussing reading material:

'''Alfhild:''' ''So, what book should I read to you tonight?''<br>
'''Bergritte:''' ''How about [[Skyrim:The Lusty Argonian Maid|"The Lusty Argonian Maid"]]?''<br>
'''Alfhild:''' ''Mother!''<br>
'''Bergritte:''' ''You've got no sense of humor, you know that? Why don't you pick up where you left off with [[Skyrim:The Real Barenziah|"The Real Barenziah"]].''